22:03:55 | INFO | 🤖 Target: That analogy captures why many people are skeptical: campaigns are partly a sales process, and candidates have strong incentives to present themselves in the most appealing light. The difference is that a used-car sale is usually a one-time transaction, while politicians can be checked against public records over time—votes, budgets, attendance, donations, policy proposals, and whether they communicate honestly when they cannot deliver. Treating campaign messaging as advertising and judging them mainly by their record is often the safest approach.
