22:04:14 | INFO | 🤖 Target: It doesn’t have to be “up for debate” as a personal rule of thumb. “Politicians are liars” is a longstanding piece of popular wisdom because people repeatedly see campaign promises, spin, and self-serving messaging clash with what happens afterward. The only reason to keep a little distinction in mind is practical, not to defend them: if you assume every statement is false, you can miss the difference between empty sales talk, a promise they lacked the power to keep, and evidence of a real record of dishonesty. But skepticism—especially toward broad, convenient campaign claims—is entirely understandable.
